@startuml direct-rialto-threading-stop-sequence
title Stop() while an injector is blocked and Rialto events are in flight

participant "AAMP control\nthread" as CT
participant "AampRialtoPlayer" as P
participant "Handshake\n(State::mu, cv)" as HS
participant "Injector\nthread" as INJ
participant "Rialto pipeline" as R
participant "Rialto event\nthread" as EV

INJ -> HS : WaitForRequest()\n(blocked, no timeout)
activate INJ

CT -> P : Stop()
activate P
note right of P : lock m_flushCallMutex\n(serialises with a deferred\nflush on an injector)
P -> P : WaitForFlushToComplete()\n(<= 5000 ms if FLUSHING)
P -> P : StopProgressTimer()\npre-roll Stop(), SetMonitorAV(nullptr)
note right of P : each timer Stop() waits for\na tick already running
P -> HS : unblockInjection("Stop")
note right of HS : generation++, gate DROPPED,\npending request answered,\ncv.notify_all()
HS --> INJ : wake: generation changed
INJ --> INJ : abort sample, return
deactivate INJ

EV -> P : OnNeedMediaData (late)
P -> HS : OnNeedData()
note right of HS : DROPPED: answered\nNO_AVAILABLE_SAMPLES\n(or dropped if no pipeline)

P -> R : stop()
P -> P : SetPipeline(nullptr)\nReleaseControlBackend()
note right of P : later events see a null\npipeline snapshot and\ndo nothing
P -> P : controller Reset("Stop")\nClearForNewSession()
P -> P : stateMachine.onStop() -> IDLE
P --> CT : return
deactivate P

note over CT, EV
  The client event sink is cleared only in ~AampRialtoPlayer, after the last
  pipeline release has joined Rialto's event thread.  AAMP core must call
  UnblockTrackInjection() (StopTrackInjection) before joining an injector.
end note
@enduml
